<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>Address resolution</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Operations</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">Address resolution</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>Address resolution</strong> is the payment-grade discipline of classifying, validating, correcting and rendering postal addresses into compliant ISO 20022 structures — distinct from postal validation, which merely confirms deliverability. Deterministic engines built on <strong>RETE-style rule networks</strong> produce identical output for identical input, a prerequisite for sanctions screening and audit.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How Address resolution works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>RETE is the classic pattern-matching algorithm for production rule systems: rules compile into a discrimination network so thousands of conditions evaluate efficiently and — crucially — deterministically. That is the architectural opposite of probabilistic LLM parsing, which can produce different output for the same input. ioNova ARS applies a deterministic rules engine across 246 countries, with every verdict carrying a rule citation and audit trail.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: ioNova compare hub (deterministic vs LLM parsing); dev.ionova.ai (Classify · Validate · Correct · Render pipeline).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/purpose-built-address-solution">A purpose-built ISO 20022 address solution</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
